	// the credential typed again (the permission catalogue, ONPLO-4031). It follows
	// `changeCustomApiAddress`, because an MCP server is reached and signed in to as a Custom API is.
	//
	// THE WHOLE OF IT IS SENT, and replaces what was there: the address, the sign-in choice, and what
	// that choice asks for, the secret among them. Nothing of a credential is carried over.
	//
	// THE CONNECTION STAYS, THE KEYS ENTRY IS NEW. The credential becomes a new Keys entry bound to
	// the new address, and the old one goes to Keys' Trash. So `credential_key_id` moves, and is
	// `null` when the new sign-in choice is `none`, which keeps no credential.
