	//
	// WHAT IS PASTED IS SAID PER PRODUCT (decision 0762): one admin key for an Anthropic or OpenAI
	// organisation; an instance address, a client ID and a client secret for Jamf; an instance
	// address and one token for Kandji. The one secret is `admin_key`, and the rest are `fields`,
	// named by the system's entry in the list of systems that can be governed.
	//
	// A SYSTEM THAT IS APPROVED ANOTHER WAY IS REFUSED (422 naming `system_id`): Google Workspace,
	// Microsoft 365, a GitHub organisation and Microsoft Intune use their own admin consent
	// screen, which starts with `POST /governed-system-authorizations`. A cloud account grants a
	// role and holds no key: `POST /governed-system-roles`.
	//
	// A BUSINESS ENVIRONMENT'S ALONE. In a personal environment there is no company directory to
	// oversee, and the permission is not offered there.
	//
	// WHERE THE KEY MAY BE PRESENTED IS BOUND WHEN IT IS MADE (decision 0724): an AI provider's own
	// organisation API, or a device manager's instance at the address typed in `fields`. An instance
	// address that is not an https address alone — a path, a user, a query or a fragment — is
	// refused (422 naming `fields`, `instance_address_not_an_address_alone`).
	//
	// IT READS WORKING, NOT CHECKED YET: saving keeps the key and calls nobody (decision 0715).
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /governed-systems (the `ConnectGovernedSystemWithAdminKey` operationId).
