// RotateAccessKeyWithBody Rotate an access key's secret
//
// A new secret for the same key: its name, what it may reach and its end stand, and so
// do its machine's grants, seat and audit continuity (security baseline §3.20, Acceptance).
// The old secret stops at once. The new one is in this answer and in no other, as at minting.
// Its end stays as it is, so a rotation for a leak is one press. A key whose end has
// passed is refused `422`: it is minted again, never rotated back to life.
//
