// StartConnectionReauthorization Start reconnecting an OAuth connection
//
// RECONNECT, for an OAuth connection that is disconnected, expiring or no longer working. It
// answers the address of the provider's own consent screen; the connection keeps its id, its
// owner and everything that uses it, and only the grant behind it is renewed.
//
// A connection of another kind holds a credential you typed, and is refused here with
// `connection_kind_mismatch` — enter that credential again instead.
//
// A ROW THAT READS WORKING IS REFUSED with `connection_still_working`. Reconnect is offered on
// a row that reads DISCONNECTED, NOT WORKING or EXPIRING, "as on every connection, and never on
// one that reads WORKING: there is nothing to mend, and a second approval would only replace a
// credential that works."
//
// A PAUSED OR A STOPPED CONNECTION IS REFUSED, for everybody, a company admin included:
// `connection_paused` while its owner is suspended, `connection_stopped` once its company is
// closed. Reconnecting would replace the credential of a person the company has suspended.
//
// NOTHING IS RENEWED YET. The grant is renewed once the person has approved again and the
// provider's answer is handed in, with `completion`. A reconnect nobody finishes costs nothing
// and stops working by itself, ten minutes after it starts.
//
// A SYSTEM WHOSE PROVIDER ONPLO HOLDS NO OAUTH APP OF ITS OWN AT YET answers 501: that part is
// not built, and nothing about your request is wrong (ONPLO-1824).
//
// Corresponds with POST /connections/{connection_id}/reauthorizations (the `StartConnectionReauthorization` operationId).
func (c *Client) StartConnectionReauthorization(ctx context.Context, connectionId ConnectionId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewStartConnectionReauthorizationRequest(c.Server, connectionId)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

// CompleteConnectionReauthorizationWithBody Finish reconnecting an OAuth connection
//
// The provider sends the person back with a code; hand it in here and the connection's grant
// is renewed. Its own permission is the one that started it: reconnecting is a change to a
// connection, never a new one.
//
// ONLY WHOEVER STARTED IT MAY FINISH IT, and only on the connection it was started for. To
// anybody else, and on any other connection, the reconnect does not exist.
//
// THE CONNECTION THEN READS WORKING, NOT CHECKED YET, as a connection just made does: what the
// provider granted this time replaces what it granted before. A connection paused or stopped
// since the start is refused (`connection_paused`, `connection_stopped`), and nothing is renewed.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /connections/{connection_id}/reauthorizations/{connection_authorization_id}/completion (the `CompleteConnectionReauthorization` operationId).
