// TestConnection Test a connection
//
// ONE CLICK VERIFIES THE CREDENTIALS, before anything depends on them. Onplo reaches the
// system now and answers the connection as it reads afterwards — so a test that fails is
// still a 200: the call worked, and `status` says the connection does not.
//
// A DATABASE ALSO ANSWERS ITS TABLES, so the table picker in a flow step works and you know
// it is reachable.
//
// TESTING IS ITS OWN PERMISSION, because every action is one (decision 0651, amending 0633).
// The roles that create and edit connections carry it, so whoever may edit a connection may
// still test it, in a personal and in a business environment alike. It shows a database's
// table names and spends a call at the provider, so seeing the connection is not enough.
//
// A PAUSED OR A STOPPED CONNECTION IS NOT WOKEN (ONPLO-2663). While its owner is suspended a
// connection reads NOT WORKING, "paused — its owner is suspended", and this is refused for
// everybody, a company admin included, with `connection_paused`: it would run or replace the
// credential of a person the company has suspended. Once its company is closed it reads "stopped —
// the company is closed", and this is refused with `connection_stopped`, because the grace period
// never reopens a company. Disconnect still ends either.
//
// A CONNECTION WITH AN API KEY OR A DATABASE IS TESTED. SO IS A CUSTOM API that signs in with a
// key in a header, a Bearer token or Basic (ONPLO-5214): its own test request, "GET path to verify the whole setup
// end-to-end", is sent under its base address with its default headers, and one with no test
// request reads NOT WORKING, saying so (ONPLO-2036). An OAuth connection is tested by its own
// connect flow, an outside MCP server once its address can be presented (ONPLO-4142), and a
// Custom API that signs in with nothing once the vault can present it; until then
// each answers 501 and nothing is reached (decision 0725).
//
// Corresponds with POST /connections/{connection_id}/test (the `TestConnection` operationId).
func (c *Client) TestConnection(ctx context.Context, connectionId ConnectionId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewTestConnectionRequest(c.Server, connectionId)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

