// Disconnecting one that is already disconnected changes nothing and answers the same.
//
// UNDER A LEGAL HOLD IT STILL ENDS, AND IS NEVER REFUSED FOR ONE, as a connection's Disconnect
// does (decision 0947): reading stops and the row reads DISCONNECTED, and a credential a hold
// covers is kept, unusable and unreadable, and destroyed when the hold is released.
