// MakeMachineWithBody Make a machine — the identity its access keys belong to
//
// A MACHINE IS A STANDING NON-HUMAN IDENTITY: "a connected computer, a CI pipeline, a vendor's
// integration". "You make it here with a handle, a steward, a pinned role and its caps, and
// then mint one or more keys for it." Its keys are only passes: "rotating or revoking one
// never touches the machine's grants, seat or history".
//
// IDENTITY KEEPS IT. A machine is identity's, "its handle, its pinned role and its steward"
// (the data-ownership register), and its build scopes are kept on that same record (decision
// 0843). This operation is its face, and Integrations keeps no copy of those four. It is
// listed and seated in Account → Manage users → Machines, which reads `listMachineIdentities`.
// Its seat is assigned there by hand, by whoever holds the permission; making it takes none
// (the owner's ruling of 16 November 2026, ONPLO-3824).
//
// BUILD SCOPES ARE TICKED NOW OR NEVER: "Ticked here, at creation, or never". Each is a
// ring-2 permission of the catalogue, and nothing changes them afterwards (decision 0843,
// rule 2). One that is not a ring-2 permission is refused `422`.
//
// ITS CAPS ARE TAKEN IN THE SAME FORM, and Integrations keeps them, never identity (decision
// 0885). They are the fields `setMachineCaps` takes, each left out or `null` for no cap, and
// the answer carries both as they were kept. Integrations keeps its record of the machine
// once identity has made it; sending the same request again keeps the caps first kept.
//
// A MONTHLY BUDGET IS IN EUROS, with exactly two decimals. One in another currency is
// refused `422` at `/body/per_month_budget/currency`, and one with other decimals at
// `/body/per_month_budget/amount`, before anything is made.
//
// WHAT IDENTITY WOULD NOT MAKE IS REFUSED, AND NOTHING IS MADE. A handle taken is `409`. A
// steward who is no member or team here, a role this environment does not have, a role that
// reaches a permission the caller does not hold here, and a build scope that is no ring-2
// permission are each `422`, naming the field, with identity's word in `errors[].code`.
// Sending the same four again answers the machine already made.
//
// THE FULL HANDLE NAMES THE COMPANY. `handle` is `@<company>/machine/<handle_name>`, the
// company's @ name asked of Account once the machine is made (ONPLO-3456). A company with no @
// name yet, or Account that could not be asked, leaves `handle` out and answers the machine
// made; sending the same four again answers it whole.
//
// ITS OWN PUBLIC KEY MAY COME WITH IT (ONPLO-5512). The machine makes its key pair itself and
// sends only the public half, `public_key`, which Keys locks its secrets to. A key whose kind
// and coordinates do not pair is refused `422` before identity is asked. Integrations keeps
// it beside the caps, and answers it back.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /machines (the `MakeMachine` operationId).
