	// NEVER MORE THAN ITS HOLDER, AND NEVER MORE THAN YOU: "scoped ≤ your Account permissions". A
	// line that reaches further is refused `422`, and so is a ring-1 permission, which no key may
	// carry. A PERSONAL KEY IS RING 3 ONLY, ALWAYS (security baseline §3.20), so a personal key
	// carrying a ring-2 permission is refused too. A machine's key may carry one only where its
	// machine was made with that build scope (decision 0843).
	//
	// THE PAGE'S "READ / WRITE / MANAGE" IS THE SCREEN'S GROUPING of these permissions, not a
	// level of its own: a key holds catalogue permissions, as every grant does, so what a key may
	// do is answered by the one catalogue and never by a second scale.
