	// WHAT ONPLO CANNOT UNDO THERE. "Onplo gives back its own token where the other system lets
	// it. A role or a key the admin made there is the admin's to delete" — Onplo can change
	// nothing in that system.
	//
	// WHAT WAS READ WAS NEVER INTEGRATIONS' TO KEEP. It "belongs to the app that asked for it,
	// and each says what it does with it". Here "Integrations itself keeps the row and the moment
	// of the last read, and nothing of what was read".
