	// delivery is erased 30 days after it arrived (decision 0453; the system map).
	//
	// A DELIVERY IS ALWAYS ACCEPTED. One that arrives "while the linked flow is paused, undeployed
	// or over quota is ACCEPTED — the sender always gets a clean OK" — and handed to Flows like any
	// other. Flows decides what happens next, and the log shows a held one as "held by Flows —
	// starts on resume", with the reason Flows gave. "Integrations keeps no second copy and offers
	// no replay of a held delivery, so nothing runs twice" (the spec lane's ruling of 28 October
	// 2026, ONPLO-3186). This said until 29 October 2026 that one click replays everything held.
	// SINCE 17 NOVEMBER 2026 A DELIVERY'S CONTENT IS KEPT 7 DAYS after every app that uses the address
	// has it, and then erased (the owner, 15 November 2026, ONPLO-3740): read one delivery with what it
	// carried (`getWebhookDelivery`). Re-sending a failed one within those 7 days is not built yet.
	//
	// A REVOKED ENDPOINT'S LOG IS READ HERE TOO, for its 30 days: "the delivery log and what was
	// already held stay for their 30 days". A revoke removes the endpoint, and this path still
	// answers its log while a delivery of its last 30 days is kept; once none is, it is the
	// endpoint's 404, as an id that names nothing is (ONPLO-3741). Until 7 November 2026 this said
	// how that log is read was not declared yet.
