// ListAccessKeysWithResponse The access keys of this environment
//
// EVERY ACCESS KEY HERE, a machine's and a person's, each with what it may reach, when it
// ends and when it was last used. Never a key's secret: "The key itself is shown ONCE, on
// creation".
//
// AN ACCESS KEY IS A DOOR INTO ONPLO, and never a Keys entry: "A KEYS ENTRY is a secret or
// named value Onplo uses to reach OUT". So the path says `/access-keys`, never a bare `key`
// (decision 0515).
//
// NOT YET HERE, each with its reason: the stale flag, because no page says after how long a
// key is stale; the data sensitivity a key inherits, because nothing classifies what a
// permission reaches yet; and MCP clients and agent-to-agent grants, the other credentials
// `machine-credential` covers, which are declared with their own pages' work.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /access-keys (the `ListAccessKeys` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ListAccessKeysWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *ListAccessKeysParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ListAccessKeysResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ListAccessKeys(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseListAccessKeysResponse(rsp)
}

// CreateAccessKeyWithBodyWithResponse Mint an access key — for a machine, or for yourself
//
// "Create a key here and pick exactly what it may reach — which resources, across one app or
// several". Each line of `reach` is one permission of the catalogue, on one object or, with no
// object, wherever that permission reaches in this environment. "One key, many things; no key
// sprawl."
//
// NEVER MORE THAN ITS HOLDER, AND NEVER MORE THAN YOU: "scoped ≤ your Account permissions". A
// line that reaches further is refused `422`, and so is a ring-1 permission, which no key may
// carry. A PERSONAL KEY IS RING 3 ONLY, ALWAYS (security baseline §3.20), so a personal key
// carrying a ring-2 permission is refused too. A machine's key may carry one only where its
// machine was made with that build scope (decision 0843).
//
// THE PAGE'S "READ / WRITE / MANAGE" IS THE SCREEN'S GROUPING of these permissions, not a
// level of its own: a key holds catalogue permissions, as every grant does, so what a key may
// do is answered by the one catalogue and never by a second scale.
//
// LEFT WITHOUT `machine_id`, IT IS A PERSONAL KEY of the person asking. A key minted from a
// member's row is not declared: a personal key carries its person's name (ONPLO-3285).
//
// EVERY KEY ENDS: "a key that never expires is the one nobody remembers to revoke" (decision
