// CreateConnectionWithBodyWithResponse Connect a system with an API key or as an app, connect a database, a Custom API, an MCP server or another phone service
//
// The six connect flows in which you TYPE the credential. `kind` says which, and each takes
// the fields of its own configuration block. An OAuth connection is not made here: you grant
// access at the provider, so it starts with `POST /connection-authorizations`.
//
// A CUSTOM API NAMES NO SYSTEM: it is "the catalogue's floor rather than an entry", so you
// say where it lives and how it is signed in to. Four of its five sign-in choices are
// connected here — none, a key in a header, a Bearer token, Basic. OAuth2 is not yet, and
// sending it is refused as a value this operation does not take (ONPLO-2036).
//
// AN OUTSIDE MCP SERVER NAMES NO SYSTEM EITHER: its HTTPS address and a name you give it,
// signing in with none, a key in a header or a Bearer token (ONPLO-3478). OAuth on the
// server's own screen is not made here yet (ONPLO-4032).
//
// GITHUB IS CONNECTED AS AN APP (`kind: app`, ONPLO-4887): the app's id, its installation's
// id and its private key, which is the credential, and optionally the repositories and the
// permissions the connection is narrowed to. Making it calls nobody, as every connect here.
//
// ANOTHER PHONE SERVICE NAMES NO SYSTEM EITHER (`kind: phone_service`, decision 0945, ONPLO-5707):
// "a connection of its own kind", for a phone service the catalogue does not list. It carries
// calls, texts or both, and "it decides which of the fields below are asked": for calls the SIP
// address with the SIP username and password, for texts the address for sending texts, the
// sign-in choice and what that choice asks for. Its text request, the incoming text fields and
// its numbers are not kept yet, so nothing it carries can be sent or received until they are
// (ONPLO-5727).
//
// THE CREDENTIAL IS WRITE-ONLY. It is visible while you type it and masked for ever after:
// it goes to the central vault as an entry in the Keys app, in this same account environment,
// and the connection that comes back carries that entry's id and never the value. Changing
// it means entering it again.
//
// THE CONNECTION IS CREATED IN THIS CREDENTIAL'S ENVIRONMENT, in the owner-scope you choose.
// `company` is refused in a personal environment (422 naming the field), which has no
// company side.
//
// THE OWNER IS A PERSON IN THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT. Left out, it is you. A company connection
// may name somebody else here, and naming somebody who is not here is refused (422 naming the
// field); whether they are is asked of the identity service, and when it cannot be asked
// nothing is made (503 `identity_unavailable`). A personal connection is yours alone, and
// naming another person for one is refused (422 naming the field).
//
// A NEW CONNECTION READS `working`, NOT CHECKED YET: `status_checked_at` is `null` until its
// first use or Test (decision 0715). Saving calls no provider.
//
// APPLE APPS AND BOOKS READS THE DATE ITS TOKEN CARRIES (decision 0837). Its `api_key` is the
// content token, the text of the file downloaded in Apple Business Manager, which names the
// date Apple ends it. A token within 30 days of that date makes the connection `expiring`,
// with the date in `expires_at`; one further away makes it `working`. A file that is no
// content token is refused (422 `content_token_unreadable` at `/body/api_key`), and so is a
// token whose date has passed (422 `content_token_ended`), which Apple takes no more. Either
// way nothing is made.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /connections (the `CreateConnection` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateConnectionWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateConnectionResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateConnectionWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateConnectionResponse(rsp)
}

