// ReplaceConnectionCredentialWithBodyWithResponse Enter a connection's credential again
//
// "Change = re-enter": the one way a typed credential changes. The new value replaces the old
// one in the same Keys entry, so `credential_key_id` does not move, and nothing that uses the
// connection has to be redeployed.
//
// FOR A CONNECTION WHOSE CREDENTIAL YOU TYPED — an API key, a database, a Custom API, an
// outside MCP server or an app. An OAuth connection holds a grant rather than something you typed, and
// is renewed by reconnecting; this operation refuses it, and refuses a body of another kind,
// with `connection_kind_mismatch`.
//
// THE BODY NAMES ITS KIND in `kind`, with the value creating a connection of that kind uses:
// `api_key`, `database`, `custom_api`, `mcp_server` or `app`. A body that names no kind, or a
// kind its fields are not, matches none of the five shapes and is refused with the 422.
//
// AN APP'S IS ITS PRIVATE KEY, AND ROTATING IT NEEDS NO RECONNECT (ONPLO-4887). GitHub lets an
// app hold more than one key at once: make a new key at GitHub, enter it here, and delete the
// old one at GitHub once the connection says the new one works. It keeps the same Keys entry.
//
// AN MCP SERVER'S IS ITS KEY OR ITS TOKEN, FOR THE SAME ADDRESS, as a Custom API's is: nothing
// else is sent, and it keeps the same Keys entry (ONPLO-4031). One that signs in with nothing
// holds no credential: `connection_kind_mismatch`.
//
// A CUSTOM API'S IS ITS KEY, ITS TOKEN OR ITS PASSWORD, FOR THE SAME ADDRESS. "Typing the
// credential again for the same address is the ordinary re-enter. It keeps the same Keys
// entry, as an API key's does." Nothing else is sent: the base URL, the sign-in choice, the
// header's name and a Basic username each say where or how the credential is sent, and none
// changes here. One that signs in with nothing holds no credential, so there is none to enter
// again: `connection_kind_mismatch`.
//
// A DISCONNECTED CONNECTION HOLDS NO CREDENTIAL, so there is none to replace: refused with
// `connection_disconnected`. Reconnecting is its own act.
//
// A PAUSED OR A STOPPED CONNECTION IS NOT WOKEN (ONPLO-2663). While its owner is suspended a
// connection reads NOT WORKING, "paused — its owner is suspended", and this is refused for
// everybody, a company admin included, with `connection_paused`: it would run or replace the
// credential of a person the company has suspended. Once its company is closed it reads "stopped —
// the company is closed", and this is refused with `connection_stopped`, because the grace period
// never reopens a company. Disconnect still ends either.
//
// AFTERWARDS THE CONNECTION READS WORKING AND NOT CHECKED YET: `status: working`, with
// `status_checked_at`, `not_working_cause` and `expires_at` all `null`. A credential just saved
// was checked by nobody, and an expiry date was the old credential's. The first use or Test
// fills it in. A connection waiting for a second person keeps reading so.
//
// APPLE APPS AND BOOKS' NEW TOKEN IS READ FOR ITS DATE (decision 0837): entered within 30 days
// of the date it carries, the connection reads `expiring`, with that date in `expires_at`. A
// file that is no content token (422 `content_token_unreadable` at `/body/api_key`), and a
// token whose date has passed (422 `content_token_ended`), replace nothing.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION. Re-entering a secret is gated apart from editing the connection it
// belongs to, so a role may rename connections without being able to replace their keys.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /connections/{connection_id}/credential (the `ReplaceConnectionCredential` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ReplaceConnectionCredentialWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, connectionId ConnectionId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ReplaceConnectionCredentialResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ReplaceConnectionCredentialWithBody(ctx, connectionId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseReplaceConnectionCredentialResponse(rsp)
}

