// SetProvisioningOutWithBodyWithResponse Turn accounts going out to Slack or GitHub on or off
//
// "On the company's Slack connection and its GitHub app, Provisioning out is a switch of its own,
// off by default, and turning it on asks that system's admin for the right to manage its users,
// because reading is all a connection holds until then." "Each system says on the switch what it
// needs on its side: Slack's paid plans that allow it, GitHub Enterprise Cloud."
//
// WHAT IT DOES ONCE ON: "a member of a team the company picks gets an account there when they
// join, a change of name or email follows, and a member who leaves Onplo, by Remove a member or
// by the identity system above, is deactivated there at the same moment." Each create, change
// and deactivation is a line in the connection's activity. "A failed call is retried, and after
// the tenth failure in a row the connection reads NOT WORKING, as every connection does, with the
// people still waiting listed."
//
// THE WHOLE OF IT IS SENT: the switch and the teams whose members get an account there. A team
// this account environment does not know is refused (422 at `/body/team_ids`,
// `provisioning_out_team_unknown`), and nothing is changed. Identity is asked which of them are
// this environment's teams; when it cannot be asked, the answer is `identity_unavailable` and
// nothing is changed, because a team nobody could check is never written down.
//
// TURNING IT ON WAITS FOR THAT SYSTEM'S ADMIN: the answer reads `waiting_for_admin_consent`, with
// the address the admin grants the right at, until they do. Turning it off stops the calls and
// closes no account there.
//
// ONLY THE SLACK CONNECTION AND THE GITHUB APP: any other connection is refused with
// `provisioning_out_not_offered`. A disconnected one is refused with `connection_disconnected`,
// and a paused or a stopped one with `connection_paused` or `connection_stopped` (ONPLO-2663).
//
// A BUSINESS ENVIRONMENT'S ALONE: the catalogue offers Set up provisioning to a company and to
// Onplo's own environment, never in a personal one.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /connections/{connection_id}/provisioning-out (the `SetProvisioningOut` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) SetProvisioningOutWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, connectionId ConnectionId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*SetProvisioningOutResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.SetProvisioningOutWithBody(ctx, connectionId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseSetProvisioningOutResponse(rsp)
}

