// DisconnectGovernedSystemWithResponse Disconnect a governed system
//
// "A governed system ends as every connection does." Disconnect "destroys Onplo's credential
// at once, reading stops at that moment, and the row reads DISCONNECTED". The row stays in
// the list, and the answer is the governed system as it now stands.
//
// WHAT ONPLO CANNOT UNDO THERE. "Onplo gives back its own token where the other system lets
// it. A role or a key the admin made there is the admin's to delete" — Onplo can change
// nothing in that system.
//
// WHAT WAS READ WAS NEVER INTEGRATIONS' TO KEEP. It "belongs to the app that asked for it,
// and each says what it does with it". Here "Integrations itself keeps the row and the moment
// of the last read, and nothing of what was read".
//
// Disconnecting one that is already disconnected changes nothing and answers the same.
//
// UNDER A LEGAL HOLD IT STILL ENDS, AND IS NEVER REFUSED FOR ONE, as a connection's Disconnect
// does (decision 0947): reading stops and the row reads DISCONNECTED, and a credential a hold
// covers is kept, unusable and unreadable, and destroyed when the hold is released.
// `kept_by_legal_hold` carries the one thing that differs.
//
// A STOP, NEVER A REMOVAL (decision 0765): "Disconnect moves to the same act a connection's
// has, still inside Manage governed systems, and the deletion is Remove". Taking the row away
// is `DELETE` on the governed system, and Reconnect in place has its own three operations.
//
// THIS ASKED FOR THE DELETION'S PERMISSION UNTIL 12 OCTOBER 2026, because the catalogue wrote
// Disconnect as a deletion. It asks for the stop's now, `integrations:governed-system.suspend`,
// as a connection's Disconnect does.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /governed-systems/{governed_system_id}/disconnection (the `DisconnectGovernedSystem` operationId).
