// ListUsageLogLinesWithResponse What crossed the boundary
//
// "Audit of everything that crossed the boundary": one line for each call Onplo made, or
// stopped, through a connection of this account environment, newest first — "which
// connection, by which app/flow/agent, on whose behalf, when, result".
//
// A LENS, NEVER A SECOND LOG. "Written by the one append-only audit log and read here.
// Integrations never keeps a second log, and the same records appear in Account → Activity."
// So every field of a line is the audit service's to answer, and its read is not in a
// contract yet.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION. "The page is read by whoever holds View usage logs. It is a permission
// of its own and no part of View connections, because a line names the flow or agent that
// made the call and on whose behalf, which is more than a connection's row shows. A plan
// never decides who reads it; the permission does."
//
// `owner_scope` IS THE MY / COMPANY FILTER, which "narrows by the connection a call went
// through. My shows the calls through your own connections; Company shows the calls through
// the company's … so a call is on exactly one side. A personal account environment has no
// company side and shows no filter." THE PERSONAL SIDE IS YOURS ALONE, as the personal
// connections are: a call through another person's own connection is on nobody else's page.
//
// HOW FAR BACK IS THE LOG'S ANSWER, NEVER THIS APP'S. "This page shows everything the
// platform audit log still holds, which is the platform's own retention and not this app's;
// there is no free window, no Premium window".
//
// NOT HERE: the role a line is "tied to" — the session's scope at the moment of the call,
// which no writer of an audit event is told yet (ONPLO-1209). Nor a count of calls this
// month beside a connection's budget, which no page puts on this page.
//
// **NOT SERVED YET — it answers 501 until the service is built (ONPLO-1071).**
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
