// ListWebhookDeliveriesWithResponse What reached a webhook endpoint
//
// THE DELIVERY LOG, newest first: when each delivery arrived, whether it started the flow or
// was held, and which signing secret verified it — "which secret each delivery used". Seeing
// what arrived is the free core: "visibility is never paid". Integrations holds it, and a
// delivery is erased 30 days after it arrived (decision 0453; the system map).
//
// A DELIVERY IS ALWAYS ACCEPTED. One that arrives "while the linked flow is paused, undeployed
// or over quota is ACCEPTED — the sender always gets a clean OK" — and handed to Flows like any
// other. Flows decides what happens next, and the log shows a held one as "held by Flows —
// starts on resume", with the reason Flows gave. "Integrations keeps no second copy and offers
// no replay of a held delivery, so nothing runs twice" (the spec lane's ruling of 28 October
// 2026, ONPLO-3186). This said until 29 October 2026 that one click replays everything held.
// SINCE 17 NOVEMBER 2026 A DELIVERY'S CONTENT IS KEPT 7 DAYS after every app that uses the address
// has it, and then erased (the owner, 15 November 2026, ONPLO-3740): read one delivery with what it
// carried (`getWebhookDelivery`). Re-sending a failed one within those 7 days is not built yet.
//
// A REVOKED ENDPOINT'S LOG IS READ HERE TOO, for its 30 days: "the delivery log and what was
// already held stay for their 30 days". A revoke removes the endpoint, and this path still
// answers its log while a delivery of its last 30 days is kept; once none is, it is the
// endpoint's 404, as an id that names nothing is (ONPLO-3741). Until 7 November 2026 this said
// how that log is read was not declared yet.
//
// A REFUSAL IS LOGGED TOO. One over 5 MiB, or whose signature did not verify, started nothing,
// and its row says so, with no payload; refusals from one sender within a minute collapse into
// one row with a count (the spec lane's ruling of 29 October 2026, ONPLO-3737).
//
// NOT HERE: a delivery's content. One delivery is read with what it carried, while it is kept
// (`getWebhookDelivery`, ONPLO-3740). Until 17 November 2026 this said where it is kept was not
// ruled.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /webhook-endpoints/{webhook_endpoint_id}/deliveries (the `ListWebhookDeliveries` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ListWebhookDeliveriesWithResponse(ctx context.Context, webhookEndpointId WebhookEndpointId, params *ListWebhookDeliveriesParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ListWebhookDeliveriesResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ListWebhookDeliveries(ctx, webhookEndpointId, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseListWebhookDeliveriesResponse(rsp)
}

// GetWebhookDeliveryWithResponse One delivery, with what it carried
//
// ONE LINE OF THE DELIVERY LOG, AND ITS CONTENT WHILE IT IS KEPT. "Inspect deliveries and payloads —
// seeing what arrived is part of the free core (visibility is never paid)."
//
// THE CONTENT IS KEPT 7 DAYS, THE LINE 30 (the owner, 15 November 2026, ONPLO-3740): "a message's
// content stays until every app that uses the address has it, plus 7 days to replay a failed one,
// and is then erased". Flows is the one app that uses an address today, and a line is written once
// Flows has answered, so the content is kept until 7 days after its line was written. Then it is
// erased and the line says so (`content.state` is `erased`); the line itself stays its 30 days.
//
// A REFUSAL KEEPS NO CONTENT, and neither does a line written before 17 November 2026, when content
// began to be kept: both read `not_kept`.
//
// THE CONTENT IS THE ONE JSON OBJECT HANDED TO THE FLOW: a JSON body as the text received, a form
// as the object its fields were made into. It is the environment's, as the endpoint is, and goes
// with it. A payload may hold personal data that names nobody Onplo can find in it, so a person's
// erasure cannot pick it out; its 7 days are its end.
//
// A REVOKED ENDPOINT'S DELIVERY IS READ HERE TOO, for its line's 30 days, as the log is
// (`listWebhookDeliveries`). A delivery this endpoint's log does not hold — another endpoint's,
// another environment's, or older than 30 days — is the 404.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /webhook-endpoints/{webhook_endpoint_id}/deliveries/{webhook_delivery_id} (the `GetWebhookDelivery` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) GetWebhookDeliveryWithResponse(ctx context.Context, webhookEndpointId WebhookEndpointId, webhookDeliveryId WebhookDeliveryId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*GetWebhookDeliveryResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.GetWebhookDelivery(ctx, webhookEndpointId, webhookDeliveryId, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseGetWebhookDeliveryResponse(rsp)
}

// PasteWebhookSigningSecretWithBodyWithResponse Paste the signing secret a sender shows
//
// STRIPE, SHOPIFY AND LINEAR MAKE THEIR OWN SECRET, so the person pastes the one the sender shows. Until
// one is pasted the endpoint refuses every delivery, and its log says "refused: no secret pasted
// yet" (the webhook endpoint's page, ONPLO-3738).
